{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013g5LrmRYmPVLJfRed8HE4k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Ghost World Labs / Agentic-Home â€” what this project is** (grounded in `CLAUDE.md` at the workspace root):\n\n- **It's a research workspace, not a production system.** John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\" for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. Most of the ~80 root markdown files are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs); a smaller subset is runnable code.\n\n- **The active shipped deliverable is the GWL master GUI** â€” a Next.js app in `sandbox-lab-gui/` (custom Next.js + WebSocket server, `server.mjs`) that launches and supervises agents. Entry point is `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`, runs on `localhost:3001`, pre-creates `gemini` / `claude` / `alpha` terminals.\n\n- **Agents run on the OpenClaw runtime** (MIT-licensed, global npm install). The GUI dispatches to it via `agent-chat.mjs`, with a canonical agent registry/routing in `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`. The daily-use vehicle is `alpha-v0` (a t2r agent through `t2r-dispatcher.mjs`); other agents are research/legacy or planned-but-unbuilt.\n\n- **The core architecture bet is \"distill from frontier into small local students\"** â€” a t2r (\"taste â†’ reason\") brain plus a custom **harness** that's deliberately *brain-agnostic* (Opus-4.8, t2r, or a fully-local ~7â€“8B sovereign brain all plug in). Hardware is the gwl-server box (RTX 4070, 12 GB), bounding training to QLoRA on â‰¤8B models.\n\n- **A skill ecosystem feeds it** â€” a master skill repo (`skills-master/`) linked into Claude Code / Gemini / OpenClaw, with skills like `expert-coder`, `deep-research`, `project-manager`, `crucible`, `foreman`.\n\n- **Current active work** (per \"Recently completed\") is harness completion: M1 is feature-complete for google+anthropic, and a Crucible-forged, Foreman-ready multi-wave plan drives the path to GA. Recent commits on `foreman/run` shipped default-OFF flag-gated harness features (verify workers, approval gates, replanning, command sandbox).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: these claims come from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and memory index, not from independently reading the code. If you want, I can verify a specific claim (e.g., that `sandbox-lab-gui/` actually builds/runs, or that the routing/agent files exist as described) against the filesystem."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7053,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6be5e03-ea72-40dc-bcaa-dbbceb036ffe","uuid":"e3e4b7ba-c063-4fa9-9eb6-dcd69bb97f09","request_id":"req_011Cc3tiBt9RaQxTisD81fdH"}
